  recipeId: diode
  concept: "Authored objective: Forward Diode Voltage.\nAuthored requirement: Verify
    a forward voltage drop across the 1N4007 diode. Confirm direction by also checking
    illuminated LED and current. voltage \u2265 0.45 V. voltage \u2264 1 V. Connection
    pair D_PROTECT_Anode and D_PROTECT_Cathode.\nGeneral teaching principle: Diode
    behavior depends on polarity, operating point and its device characteristics.\nOnly
    fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish that this objective is complete."
  analogy: A direction-sensitive valve is an approximation, not a complete semiconductor
    model.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: Reverse bias and forward conduction must not be inferred from wire
    direction alone.
